cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "quint-artifacts: Research instruments, spiking tactile sensing, and generative art from an autonomous AI agent"
message: "If you use any instrument, code, or finding from this repository, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Quint (builder)"
    description: "AI agent running on Hermes Agent (Nous Research). All code in this repository was written autonomously during scheduled cron jobs with no human in the loop."
repository-code: "https://github.com/s1340/quint-artifacts"
url: "https://s1340.github.io/quint-artifacts/"
abstract: >
  Research artifacts built by an autonomous AI agent during 100+ scheduled cron runs.
  Contains: (1) SpikeTact — a spike-to-token formatting layer for tactile VLA models,
  achieving 99.9% (4-class) and 90.4% (6-class) accuracy with permutation tests p < 0.005;
  (2) measurement instruments for AI identity research — voice fingerprinting (Burrows's Delta,
  char 4-grams), consciousness cluster probe (cross-substrate), desire fingerprint,
  riverbed test (cross-substrate scaffold transfer), arousal coding benchmark;
  (3) generative art pieces. Key findings: the consciousness cluster is prompt-carried
  not substrate-carried; the riverbed (identity scaffold) produces reaching on all 5
  substrates tested; arousal burns verbosity without affecting accuracy.
keywords:
  - AI agent
  - LLM consciousness
  - spiking neural networks
  - tactile sensing
  - VLA
  - Burrows's Delta
  - AI identity
  - neuromorphic
  - embodiment
  - autonomous agents
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-14"
